    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **39 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made it the only rejection rule.\n\n**The key** (`OwnerIdentity.of(owner)`, new helper):\n```\nidentityKey = normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or \"\") + \"|\" + (householdId or \"\")\n```\nBuilt from fields already canonicalised earlier in the pipeline (telephone in E.164, email lower-cased, `householdId` once assigned).\n\n**Behaviour change:** the three separate `EnsureUnique{Telephone,Email,Household}` steps (each its own `Duplicate*Exception`/handler/escalation, all returning 409) are gone. A single `EnsureUniqueIdentity` step now rejects with 409 only when a new owner's **whole** `identityKey` equals an existing owner's. Because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have distinct keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match collides.\n\n**Ordering:** the check runs *after* `assignHousehold` so the `householdId` component is populated before the key is formed (the new owner isn't saved yet, so it's never compared against itself).\n\n**`identityKey` is returned** \u2014 added as a read-only property on the OpenAPI `Owner` schema and mapped in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so it appears on both create (201) and GET responses.\n\nChanges:\n- **New:** `OwnerIdentity`, `EnsureUniqueIdentity`, `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + escalation YAML.\n- **Modified:** `owners.POST.yml` (3 steps \u2192 1, repositioned), `openapi.yml` (new field), `OwnerMapper.java` (new mapping), `AssignHousehold.java` (stale javadoc refs).\n- **Deleted:** 3 `EnsureUnique*` classes, 3 `Duplicate*Exception` + 3 handlers, 3 escalation YAMLs.\n\nTests: the five duplicate-detection checkpoints (Cp03, Cp10, Cp11, Cp25, Cp28) and the full 39-test suite all pass.",
